### Variables
@host = http://localhost:4004
@service = {{host}}/procurement

### 1. List vendors
GET {{service}}/Vendors
Accept: application/json

### 2. List products
GET {{service}}/Products
Accept: application/json

### 3. List purchase requests
GET {{service}}/PurchaseRequests
Accept: application/json

### 4. Check approver for an amount (Manager tier)
GET {{service}}/getRequiredApprover(amount=750)
Accept: application/json

### 5. Check approver for a larger amount (Director tier)
GET {{service}}/getRequiredApprover(amount=6000)
Accept: application/json

### 6. Create a new Draft request (omit totalAmount, server computes it)
POST {{service}}/PurchaseRequests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "requestedBy": "Mohamed Test",
  "vendor_ID": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "product_ID": "aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa",
  "quantity": 5,
  "notes": "Test request created via REST"
}

### 7. List requests again - the new one should be there with totalAmount auto-computed
GET {{service}}/PurchaseRequests?$top=10
Accept: application/json

### 8. Try illegal status transition - should FAIL with 400
PATCH {{service}}/PurchaseRequests(77777777-7777-7777-7777-777777777777)
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "Closed"
}

### 9. Submit the Draft request 99999999 - large amount goes to Pending
POST {{service}}/PurchaseRequests(99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999)/ProcurementService.submit
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 10. Approve the Pending request 77777777
POST {{service}}/PurchaseRequests(77777777-7777-7777-7777-777777777777)/ProcurementService.approve
Content-Type: application/json

{}
